# Application Kconfig for the tc_uart sample. Zephyr sources the
# application-root Kconfig automatically; `source "Kconfig.zephyr"`
# keeps every base symbol available so prj.conf still works.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"

config FSW_PUS3_HK_PERIOD_SEC
	int "PUS-3 housekeeping report period (seconds)"
	default 5
	range 1 86400
	help
	  Initial value of datapool parameter 0x0001 — the interval between
	  spontaneous PUS-3[25] housekeeping parameter reports emitted by
	  the main loop. The cadence is a coarse main-loop elapsed-time
	  check against the FSW clock (k_uptime_get()/1000), not a kernel
	  timer. As of slice fsw-9 the period is a live-tunable datapool
	  parameter: a PUS-20[3] set retunes the cadence with no rebuild,
	  and a value of 0 disables periodic housekeeping. This symbol only
	  seeds the initial value. The default (5 s) is operationally sane.
	  The Renode closed-loop suite builds two
	  artefacts from this one sample: the verification-stream ELF pins
	  this to 86400 (effectively "never within a test" — Renode
	  fast-forwards idle virtual time, so a fixed short period would
	  race the fixed-offset reads non-deterministically), and a
	  dedicated housekeeping ELF pins it to 2 s for fast, deterministic
	  cadence assertions.

config FSW_FDIR_EVENT_FIFO_CAPACITY
	int "FDIR event FIFO capacity (records)"
	default 16
	range 4 256
	help
	  Number of records the bounded FDIR event FIFO holds before it
	  starts dropping the newest (the causal head — the first faults —
	  is preserved). Wired into the freestanding lib via the
	  MIGRIS_FDIR_EVENT_FIFO_CAPACITY compile definition so flight and
	  host builds size the ring identically. The default (16) absorbs a
	  burst of rejected TCs plus RX-overflow events between main-loop
	  drains; raise it only if a producer can outpace one drain per
	  loop iteration.

config FSW_DATAPOOL_CAPACITY
	int "Parameter datapool capacity (parameters)"
	default 8
	range 1 256
	help
	  Number of parameters the on-board datapool can hold. Wired into
	  the freestanding lib via the MIGRIS_DATAPOOL_CAPACITY compile
	  definition so flight and host builds size the store identically.
	  This sample registers a single parameter (the housekeeping
	  period); the default (8) leaves room for a mission to add more.

config FSW_PUS20_MAX_PARAMS
	int "PUS-20 maximum parameters per TC"
	default 8
	range 1 8
	help
	  Upper bound on the parameters one PUS-20 TC may address and one
	  [20,2] report may carry. Wired into the freestanding lib via the
	  MIGRIS_PUS20_MAX_PARAMS_PER_TC compile definition; it bounds the
	  worst-case [20,2] packet. Capped at 8 here because the TC router
	  output buffer (MIGRIS_TC_ROUTER_MAX_TM, a fixed 128) is sized for
	  that worst case — a larger value needs that constant raised too.
